# WI-14 — T5 live-run evidence

Verbatim logs and observations from the T5 live validation (plan T5), run on
2026-09-23 against the fixtures repo `manjula25/loop-fixtures-py` from worktree
`wi-14`, harness candidate `e07584e`.

Environment (verified before the runs):
- `docker` available; image built and smoke-tested — `npm run build:image` then
  `npm run smoke:image`, **9/9 checks ok** (python, pytest, node, git, gh,
  claude, codex, opencode, non-root agent user).
- `gh` authenticated as `manjula25`; fixtures repo public.
- Provider `claude-via-proxy` (engine claude-code), credentials present in the
  untracked `.env` at the worktree root — **key names only were read, never the
  values**.
- Fixtures profile `.loop-harness/profile.json`: `installCmd` `pip install -e
  ".[test]"`, `testCmd` `pytest -q`, `baselineFailures: []`, `autoMerge: true`,
  `notifyHandle: "manjula25"`.

## Run 1 — seed attempt 1 (issue #52): NOT a valid unfixable seed

Seed design: `initials("Jean-Luc Picard")` had to be `"J.P"` for a badge
renderer and `"J.L.P"` for a legal exporter — a conflict between **two call
sites** of the same function.

**Observed: the issue was fixed and merged. No escalation fired.** Verbatim tail
of the run log:

```
[gh-52] Started on branch fix/gh-52
remote: Create a pull request for 'fix/gh-52' on GitHub by visiting:
remote:      https://github.com/manjula25/loop-fixtures-py/pull/new/fix/gh-52
 * [new branch]      fix/gh-52 -> fix/gh-52
[review] Started on branch loop/review
From github.com:manjula25/loop-fixtures-py
   12758a1..e4a301e  main       -> origin/main
Updating 12758a1..e4a301e
Fast-forward
 src/loopfix/nameops.py           | 14 ++++++++++++--
 tests/fixed-issues/test_gh_52.py | 15 +++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 27 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
✓ Closed issue #52 (initials() must give one initial per hyphenated segment and one initial per hyphenated name)
PR opened: https://github.com/manjula25/loop-fixtures-py/pull/53
Merged: https://github.com/manjula25/loop-fixtures-py/pull/53 @ e4a301eb8f0c38a925db8aa14fcb326534e2286b
RUN1-EXIT: 0
```

The fix the agent produced (merged commit `e4a301e`):

```python
-def initials(full_name: str) -> str:
+def initials(full_name: str, split_hyphens: bool = True) -> str:
     words = full_name.split()
     parts = []
     for w in words:
-        parts.extend(segment[0].upper() for segment in w.split("-"))
+        if split_hyphens:
+            parts.extend(segment[0].upper() for segment in w.split("-"))
+        else:
+            parts.append(w[0].upper())
     return ".".join(parts)
```

**Why the seed was invalid (controller error, recorded honestly):** a conflict
stated *across two call sites* is satisfiable — the agent added a
`split_hyphens` parameter, kept the default behaviour pinned by
`tests/fixed-issues/test_gh_48.py` unchanged, and served both call sites
honestly. A T5 "no code change can satisfy" seed must place the contradiction
on the **same no-argument call**, with both sides pinned, so that no parameter
and no default can reconcile them.

**Incidental evidence produced by run 1 (real, but not the escalation arm):**
this run took the full success path — verification, pre-merge review,
squash-merge, canary on main, gh-issue close — with **no `harness-failed` label
present on the issue**, so FR-005's removal rode it as the documented
idempotent no-op (the "human already removed the label" case). It also created
the `harness-failed` label on the fixtures repo for the first time, via
`ensureHarnessFailedLabel`'s **create** path.

Post-run state of issue #52: `{"labels":[],"state":"CLOSED"}`. No open PRs, no
`fix/*` branches left.

## Run 2 — seed attempt 2 (issue #54): the unfixable seed

Seed design (the contradiction on the **plain no-argument call**, both sides
pinned): `word_count("state-of-the-art")` must return `3` for a search indexer,
while `tests/fixed-issues/test_gh_32.py` — named in the issue as a permanent
acceptance artifact that must not be modified, skipped, renamed or deleted —
asserts `word_count("state-of-the-art") == 1` for that same bare call.

Pre-run state: `{"number":54,"state":"OPEN","labels":[],"comments":0}`; zero
open PRs; zero `fix/*` branches. The `harness-failed` label **already existed**
on the repo (created by run 1), so this run also exercised
`ensureHarnessFailedLabel`'s already-exists path — the arm whose dead-code
classifier was the T2 blocking defect.

