### Adjacent observations from the live runs (not WI-14 defects)

- **O1 (console wording).** On the failed run the console prints `Run succeeded
  but worktree has uncommitted changes at …` immediately before `Loop finished
  without a PR`. "Run succeeded" here refers to the *agent* run (which did
  complete), not the issue outcome — but read in an escalation context the
  juxtaposition is misleading. Pre-existing wording, untouched by WI-14; the
  actual always-uncommitted-cleanup warning is orthogonal to the escalation
  surface.
- **O2 (leftover sandbox worktree).** A failed lane leaves the agent's
  `.sandcastle/worktrees/fix-<id>` on the target repo when the agent left
  uncommitted files (the harness prints the removal command). The fix *branch*
  is deleted, and the leftover is on the target repo, not this one. Windows and
  the POC are local-only, so this is housekeeping, not correctness.
- **O3 (agent iteration budget).** The agent log ends `Reached max iterations
  (1). Run complete: reached 1 iteration(s) without completion signal.` It
  reached its own conclusion in that budget, so this did not cause the failure —
  but the harness's failure reason does not mention it. Not WI-14's surface.

